            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for a detailed issue!\r\n\r\nIt seems like symptoms of asynchronous nature of scroll. When you execute `<C-d>zz` mapping, what happens is Neovim registers `<C-d>` and 'mini.animate' starts scroll animation (which also progressively changes cursor position for a smoother effect). **But** right after it start animating, there is a `zz` command which is registered as another scroll event which takes precedence (thus trying to center the screen).\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, having multiple scrolling commands in a mapping is not really supported. The best way to overcome this right now is by following [this advice](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/212#issuecomment-1411674528). Could you try remapping it as written there and tell if this makes things better?",
            "created_at": "2023-02-15T08:27:22Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/228#issuecomment-1430932616",
